<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Noor Mahal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1872–1875</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Noor Mahal is a palace in Bahawalpur, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, built for Nawab Sadiq Muhammad Khan IV between 1872 and 1875. Designed in an Italianate style with Islamic domes, it served as a state guest house and a venue for the nawabs' durbars and official receptions. It is now owned by the Pakistan Army and is open to visitors as a heritage site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/noor-mahal.jpg" alt="Noor Mahal" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Muhammad Ashar · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Front_Elevation_of_Noor_Mahal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
